    {
      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The carrier equation separates dense feature construction from window partitioning, and the partition keeps the tokens rather than replacing them.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder maps the low-resolution image into a dense feature field. That field is the persistent carrier needed by super-resolution. The window operation partitions the field into tokens. The equation keeps the dense carrier visible while the compact thought process reads and updates it.",
